// axverity-readtier.axreg — AXVERITY_READ_INDEX_RAM_TIER_V1.
//
// A registry of its own, deliberately NOT merged into
// registries/axverity-working2.axreg. UNWIRED_BY_DESIGN is a structural
// property here, not a promise: the read tier links into its own binary
// (readtier/build/rt-driver) from its own sources, declares no channel that
// any wp_* fn names, and the write path's build (scripts/build.sh) never
// reads this file. There is no edge between the two graphs to accidentally
// close.
//
// Every fn below is kind leaf; bodies resolve via --lib-dir readtier/lib_coreir
// at link time. identity = sha256(utf8(name)), nothing else.
//
// No `channel` block appears in this file. The read tier is single-writer and
// single-threaded; its cross-call state lives in the bridge's named scratch
// maps (scratch.rs), which are thread-local by construction. Nothing here can
// be reached from another thread, so there is nothing to lock.
//
// `idempotent` ON EVERY FN BELOW IS UNVERIFIED PROSE. Nothing reads it. The
// compiler's hash-cons shareability test is `effect_class == Pure &&
// deterministic` and nothing else (axis-lang/src/ir/core_ir_05.rs,
// push_node), so an idempotent line changes no behaviour anywhere. It is a
// DECLARATION and is kept as one — declaration-versus-enforcement is a real
// distinction and the field is still worth stating truthfully — but do not
// reason from these values as though something checked them.
//
// `effect` and `deterministic`, by contrast, ARE load-bearing: declaring a
// genuinely effectful fn pure+deterministic lets CCall CSE merge two calls into
// one, which is how the write path's real packing loop once ceased to exist.
//
// Generated by scripts/regen-readtier-reg.sh — edit that, not this.

registry axverity-readtier 0.1

